# A fetched stylesheet's bytes are decoded into text once for the page.
# sheet-cache.html links one sheet and then adds three <style> elements by
# script, a task apart, so the shell collects the page's sheets again for
# each (five collections in all here, the page's first frame and its
# parse counted); the linked sheet's bytes come back from the cache each
# time and are decoded on the first collection alone, and its rule still
# applies at the end. The wait is stepped: each step runs the timers due.
resize 800 600
open sheet-cache.html
advance 100
advance 100
advance 100
advance 100
assert-title added 3 rgb(1, 2, 3)
assert-sheet-collections 5
assert-sheet-decodes 1
